reading the table:
- saved fences = claims the governor policy did NOT pay (the FastPath
  throttle skips the poll after an unchanged frame — bounded to every
  other poll, self-correcting through framesBehind).
- saved memcpy = draw-phase payload copies the governor policy did NOT
  pay (idempotent redraws elided: FastPath + same seq).
- deliv = distinct frames drawn — a POLICY outcome: Skip(n) drops
  intermediates BY DECISION (Law 4), so the governor legitimately draws
  fewer distinct frames when behind. The GATED invariant is the
  finalSeq/writerPublished pair: each policy must end the window
  holding a frame within one poll-period (+ stop latency) of its
  writer's final published count — no stale, no lost consumer.
- Ratios are the result; absolute rates are node-sandbox numbers.
- Convergence lag bound per row: ceil(hz*(hold+25ms)) + 2 frames
  (one poll period + stop-message latency).
RESULT: PASS — content parity holds; savings recorded above
